# MANIFEST.md publishes the SHA-256 of every file as it left the builder, with LF line endings.
# A checkout that converted them to CRLF would make every one of those hashes fail on Windows, and
# a manifest that fails for a reason unrelated to tampering teaches its reader to ignore it.
# The private tree already forced LF on its sealed evidence for the same reason (M-09.1).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.docx binary
*.png binary
